IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei7-related-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): RELATED PROVISIONS of 2018, c. 12, ss. 292 to 295 (src:3841-3882):
-- the election to have earnings deducted from benefits by a different measure ($75 or 40% of the weekly rate).
-- Written by piece ei7 (Sonnet 5.5). Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
-- Seat: the claimant, asking whether they may elect, how much of the week's earnings is deducted if they do, by when
-- they must tell the Commission, whether a late election counts, and whether the Commission's decision can be
-- reconsidered.
--
-- What is out of range. "The Regulations" in ss. 293 to 295 means the Employment Insurance Regulations as they read on
-- August 11, 2018 (s. 292(2)); the elections they mention (s. 77.98, s. 77.991(2)) are in the Regulations' file,
-- which piece er5 encodes, and whether a claimant "was eligible to make" one is a BOOLEAN input here. The amount
-- "described in subsection 19(2)" (and 152.18(2)) that the election replaces is another piece's (ei1, ei5).
-- The judgment whether "good cause" was shown is the Commission's (and on appeal the Tribunal's): a BOOLEAN input
-- named for the showing, never worked out here.
-- A rate of weekly benefits is a NUMBER of dollars (section 14, piece ei1). 40% of it is not rounded: s. 6(2) rounds
-- "in this Part" and these sections are not in Part I. Fork F9.

§ `Section 292 - words and the version of the Regulations`

-- (1) "Words and expressions used in sections 293 to 295 have the same meaning as in the Employment Insurance Act" is
-- `inert`: it points at the Act's definitions, which the core already encodes (eia-core-interpretation).
-- (2) fixes the version of the Regulations as they read on August 11, 2018, a day the rules below also use.
-- src:3841 | — 2018, c. 12, s. 292
-- src:3842 | Words and expressions
-- src:3843 | 292 (1) Words and expressions used in sections 293 to 295 have the same meaning as in the Employment Insurance Act.
-- src:3844 | Definition of Regulations
-- src:3845 | (2) In sections 293 to 295, Regulations means the Employment Insurance Regulations as they read on August 11, 2018.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 292(2) (src:3845)
`Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 292(2) August 11, 2018` MEANS YearMonthDay 2018 8 11

§ `Section 293 - an election by a claimant who could have elected under the Regulations`

-- src:3847 | — 2018, c. 12, s. 293
-- src:3848 | Claimants eligible to make election
-- src:3849 | 293 (1) A claimant who was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations in respect of a benefit period and who did not, before August 12, 2018, make such an election, may, after August 11, 2018, make an election under subsection (2) in respect of that benefit period if
-- src:3850 | (a) the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of that benefit period is issued to the claimant after July 13, 2018; and
-- src:3851 | (b) the claimant receives earnings during one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period and makes a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks.
-- src:3852 | Election
-- src:3853 | (2) A claimant to whom this section applies may elect, in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment that fall in the benefit period referred to in subsection (1), to have deducted from benefits the amount, if any, of the earnings that exceeds the following instead of the amount described in subsection 19(2) of the Employment Insurance Act:
-- src:3854 | (a) $75, if the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits is less than $188; or
-- src:3855 | (b) 40% of the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits, if that rate is $188 or more.
-- src:3856 | Requirement to inform Commission
-- src:3857 | (3) A claimant must inform the Commission of their election, if any, in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period not later than the 30th day after the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period is issued to the claimant. The election is irrevocable.
-- src:3858 | Late election
-- src:3859 | (4) If a claimant informs the Commission of their election after the day on which the deadline expires, the election is considered to have been made by that deadline if the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period that begins on the day on which the deadline expired and that ends on the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election.
-- src:3860 | No reconsideration of decision
-- src:3861 | (5) A decision of the Commission in respect of any matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election, is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Employment Insurance Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 293(1) (src:3849-3851)
`Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1) August 12, 2018` MEANS YearMonthDay 2018 8 12

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 293(1)(a) (src:3850)
`Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1)(a) July 13, 2018` MEANS YearMonthDay 2018 7 13

-- (1) the claimant may, after August 11, 2018, make an election under (2) in respect of the benefit period if (a) the
-- last notification ... is issued after July 13, 2018 and (b) the claimant receives earnings in one or more weeks of
-- unemployment in it and makes a claim for at least one of those weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 293(1) (src:3849-3851)
GIVEN `the claimant was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations in respect of the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: regulation 77.991(2) (piece er5)
      `the claimant made such an election before August 12, 2018` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: regulation 77.991(2) (piece er5)
      `the day on which the claimant makes the election` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of the benefit period is issued to the claimant` IS A DATE
      `the claimant receives earnings during one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant makes a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1) the claimant may make an election under subsection (2)` IF
        `the claimant was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations in respect of the benefit period`
    AND (NOT `the claimant made such an election before August 12, 2018`)
    AND `the day on which the claimant makes the election` AT LEAST `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1) August 12, 2018`
    AND `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of the benefit period is issued to the claimant` GREATER THAN `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1)(a) July 13, 2018`
    AND `the claimant receives earnings during one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period`
    AND `the claimant makes a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks`

-- (2)(a) $75, if the claimant's rate of weekly benefits is less than $188; (b) 40% of the rate, if it is $188 or more.
-- The figures are the same in s. 295(2); this one rule serves both. "The amount, if any, of the earnings that exceeds"
-- the figure: earnings above it, and nothing when they do not exceed it. The earnings are a week's, as s. 19(2)'s
-- are. Fork F8.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 293(2), s. 295(2) (src:3854-3855) (src:3875-3876)
GIVEN `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 14, rate of weekly benefits (piece ei1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(2) and s. 295(2) the amount of a week's earnings that is not deducted` IS
    IF `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` LESS THAN 188
    THEN 75
    ELSE (40%) TIMES `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 293(2), s. 295(2) (src:3853-3855) (src:3874-3876)
GIVEN `the earnings received during the week of unemployment` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 14, rate of weekly benefits (piece ei1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(2) and s. 295(2) the amount of a week's earnings that is deducted` IS
    max 0 (`the earnings received during the week of unemployment` MINUS `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(2) and s. 295(2) the amount of a week's earnings that is not deducted` `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits`)

-- (2) a claimant to whom the section applies may elect to have this amount deducted instead of the amount under s. 19(2).
-- JUST the amount when the claimant may and does elect; NOTHING when the claimant does not, and then s. 19(2) governs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 293(2) (src:3853-3855)
GIVEN `the claimant was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations in respect of the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: regulation 77.991(2) (piece er5)
      `the claimant made such an election before August 12, 2018` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: regulation 77.991(2) (piece er5)
      `the day on which the claimant makes the election` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of the benefit period is issued to the claimant` IS A DATE
      `the claimant receives earnings during one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant makes a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant elects to have the amount deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings received during the week of unemployment` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 14, rate of weekly benefits (piece ei1)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(2) the amount of the week's earnings deducted under the election` IS
    IF     `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1) the claimant may make an election under subsection (2)` `the claimant was eligible to make an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations in respect of the benefit period` `the claimant made such an election before August 12, 2018` `the day on which the claimant makes the election` `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of the benefit period is issued to the claimant` `the claimant receives earnings during one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period` `the claimant makes a claim for benefits for at least one of those weeks`
       AND `the claimant elects to have the amount deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2)`
    THEN JUST (`Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(2) and s. 295(2) the amount of a week's earnings that is deducted` `the earnings received during the week of unemployment` `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3) the claimant must inform the Commission "not later than the 30th day after the day on which the last
