-- (5) a decision of the Commission about an election, including a failure to make one, "is not subject to
-- reconsideration under section 112": the Commission's immunity and the claimant's disability to ask. Any other
-- decision: the section says nothing, and section 112 governs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 293(5) (src:3861)
GIVEN `the decision of the Commission is in respect of a matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(5) the decision of the Commission is subject to reconsideration under section 112` IS
    IF `the decision of the Commission is in respect of a matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 294 - an election made before August 12, 2018`

-- Deemed to apply to earnings received in all weeks of unemployment included in the portion of the benefit period
-- that falls in the period August 12, 2018 to August 14, 2021. A week is identified by its Sunday; the period begins on
-- a Sunday and ends on a Saturday, so no week straddles either end (tested; fork F16).
-- src:3863 | — 2018, c. 12, s. 294
-- src:3864 | Election made before August 12, 2018
-- src:3865 | 294 An election that is made before August 12, 2018 under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations in respect of a benefit period is deemed to apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment that are included in the portion of the benefit period that falls in the period that begins on August 12, 2018 and that ends on August 14, 2021.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 294 (src:3865)
`Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 294 August 14, 2021` MEANS YearMonthDay 2021 8 14

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 294 (src:3865)
GIVEN `the day on which the election was made under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` IS A DATE  -- out of range: regulation 77.991(2) (piece er5)
      `the week of unemployment is included in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the week of unemployment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 294 the earlier election is deemed to apply to the earnings received during the week` IF
        `the day on which the election was made under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` LESS THAN `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1) August 12, 2018`
    AND `the week of unemployment is included in the benefit period`
    AND `the first day of the week of unemployment` AT LEAST `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(1) August 12, 2018`
    AND `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` `the first day of the week of unemployment` AT MOST `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 294 August 14, 2021`

§ `Section 295 - a further election, for benefit periods established up to August 14, 2021`

-- src:3867 | — 2018, c. 12, s. 295
-- src:3868 | Claimants eligible to make election
-- src:3869 | 295 (1) This section applies to
-- src:3870 | (a) a claimant who made an election under section 77.98 of the Regulations in respect of a benefit period, if the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of that benefit period was issued to them after August 6, 2016;
-- src:3871 | (b) a claimant who made an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations; and
-- src:3872 | (c) a claimant who makes an election under section 293.
-- src:3873 | Election
-- src:3874 | (2) A claimant to whom this section applies may elect, in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment before August 15, 2021 that fall in a benefit period established after August 11, 2018 but before August 15, 2021, to have deducted from benefits the amount, if any, of the earnings that exceeds the following instead of the amount described in subsection 19(2) or 152.18(2), as the case may be, of the Employment Insurance Act:
-- src:3875 | (a) $75, if the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits is less than $188; or
-- src:3876 | (b) 40% of the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits, if that rate is $188 or more.
-- src:3877 | Requirement to inform Commission
-- src:3878 | (3) A claimant must inform the Commission of their election, if any, in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a given benefit period not later than the 30th day after the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period is issued to the claimant or February 19, 2022, whichever is earlier. The election is irrevocable.
-- src:3879 | Late election
-- src:3880 | (4) If a claimant informs the Commission of their election after the day on which the deadline expires, the election is considered to have been made by that deadline if the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period that begins on the day on which the deadline expired and that ends on the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election.
-- src:3881 | No reconsideration of decision
-- src:3882 | (5) A decision of the Commission in respect of any matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election, is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Employment Insurance Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 295(1)(a) (src:3870)
`Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(1)(a) August 6, 2016` MEANS YearMonthDay 2016 8 6

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 295(2) (src:3874)
`Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(2) August 15, 2021` MEANS YearMonthDay 2021 8 15

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 295(3) (src:3878)
