-- (1) the section applies to (a) a claimant who made an election under section 77.98 of the Regulations in respect of
-- a benefit period, if the last notification in respect of it was issued after August 6, 2016; (b) a claimant who made an
-- election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations; and (c) a claimant who makes an election under section 293.
-- The three paragraphs are alternatives: "and" before (c) joins the list, and a claimant need be in only one.
-- Fork F10.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 295(1) (src:3869-3872)
GIVEN `the claimant made an election under section 77.98 of the Regulations in respect of the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: regulation 77.98 (piece er5)
      `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of that benefit period was issued to them` IS A DATE
      `the claimant made an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: regulation 77.991(2) (piece er5)
      `the claimant makes an election under section 293` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(1) section 295 applies to the claimant` IF
        (    `the claimant made an election under section 77.98 of the Regulations in respect of the benefit period`
         AND `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of that benefit period was issued to them` GREATER THAN `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(1)(a) August 6, 2016`)
    OR  `the claimant made an election under subsection 77.991(2) of the Regulations`
    OR  `the claimant makes an election under section 293`

-- (2) the election concerns earnings received during all weeks of unemployment before August 15, 2021 that fall in a
-- benefit period established after August 11, 2018 but before August 15, 2021, and replaces the amount under
-- subsection 19(2) or 152.18(2), as the case may be. A week is "before August 15, 2021" when its Saturday is. Fork F16.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 295(2) (src:3874-3876)
GIVEN `section 295 applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE  -- out of range: sections 9 and 10, when a benefit period is established (piece ei1)
      `the first day of the week of unemployment` IS A DATE
      `the claimant elects to have the amount deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2) or 152.18(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings received during the week of unemployment` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 14, rate of weekly benefits (piece ei1)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(2) the amount of the week's earnings deducted under the election` IS
    IF     `section 295 applies to the claimant`
       AND `the day on which the benefit period was established` GREATER THAN `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 292(2) August 11, 2018`
       AND `the day on which the benefit period was established` LESS THAN `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(2) August 15, 2021`
       AND `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` `the first day of the week of unemployment` LESS THAN `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(2) August 15, 2021`
       AND `the claimant elects to have the amount deducted instead of the amount under subsection 19(2) or 152.18(2)`
    THEN JUST (`Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 293(2) and s. 295(2) the amount of a week's earnings that is deducted` `the earnings received during the week of unemployment` `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3) "not later than the 30th day after the day on which the last notification ... is issued ... or February 19, 2022,
