DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(3), (4) the election is treated as made by the deadline` IF
        `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(3) the claimant informs the Commission of the election in time` `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of the benefit period is issued to the claimant` `the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of the election`
    OR  `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(4) the late election is considered to have been made by the deadline` `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of the benefit period is issued to the claimant` `the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of the election` `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period that begins on the day on which the deadline expired and that ends on the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election`

-- (5) as s. 293(5).
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 12, s. 295(5) (src:3882)
GIVEN `the decision of the Commission is in respect of a matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 12 s. 295(5) the decision of the Commission is subject to reconsideration under section 112` IS
    IF `the decision of the Commission is in respect of a matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
